      "body": "Hi! We came across NVIDIA/Megatron-LM while scanning open-source agent projects with [Trustabl](https://trustabl.ai), an open-source agent reliability scanner. It flagged a few things that may be worth a look:\n\n- **Skill processes sensitive data** (`skills/mcore-build-and-dependency/SKILL.md`): This skill's body or description names a sensitive data class — passwords, tokens, SSNs, credit card numbers, PII, or private keys — without stating what it does with that data beyond naming it.\n- **Skill processes sensitive data** (`skills/mcore-cicd/SKILL.md`): This skill's body or description names a sensitive data class — passwords, tokens, SSNs, credit card numbers, PII, or private keys — without stating what it does with that data beyond naming it.\n- **Skill processes sensitive data** (`skills/nightly-sync/SKILL.md`): This skill's body or description names a sensitive data class — passwords, tokens, SSNs, credit card numbers, PII, or private keys — without stating what it does with that data beyond naming it.\n\nThis PR adds a small GitHub Actions workflow (`.github/workflows/trustabl.yml`) so these checks run automatically:\n\n- Runs on pushes to the default branch, on pull requests, and on demand\n- Advisory only: the job uses `continue-on-error`, so it never fails your CI\n- No secrets needed; findings show up in the repo's code scanning results\n- Actions are pinned to commit SHAs, with read-only contents access\n\nSome findings may be intentional. Happy to adjust the workflow, or to close this if it's not useful.\n\nAdd Trustabl to your CI · [trustabl/trustabl-action](https://github.com/trustabl/trustabl-action) · https://trustabl.ai",
